"The System offers access to about 0.07% of people; they are called or chosen."
"Most are chosen between the ages of 15 and 17."
"About 70% are chosen after their 16th birthday and before their 17th."
"S- and A-ranks are disproportionately chosen at 15; D- and F-ranks at 17."
"Children of superhumans are much more likely to be chosen."
"Selection feels like a brief, painless full-body spasm, like a hypnic jerk."
"The System then gives its selection speech aloud, almost never as text."
"Theory holds the System reads the selectee's reactions and tweaks mind or soul as it merges."
"Selection ends a guardian's legal guardianship; the selectee is no longer a citizen."
"Until they accept, selectees have no powers affixed and feel wholly human."
